{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>תרב</b> — from the heavy [binyan], like <b>ויפן זנב אל זנב</b>." "And he said <b>my greatness</b> — corresponding to 'you have done great things.'" "And the sense of <b>you comfort me</b> — because of the troubles that had passed over him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 71, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites תרב (Psalms 71:21, 'you increase') and identifies its binyan as heavy (piel), comparing the pattern of 'he turned tail to tail' — an apparent phrase, but no such verse exists; possibly a paraphrase of Exodus or a corrupt citation.", 1 "An implied cross-reference, likely to Psalms 71:19 where the same root גדל appears."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:55.951366634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}